WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.108 --> 00:00:02.069
- I love the Weekender!
(audience applauding)

00:00:02.069 --> 00:00:02.902
All right,

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.620
let's give everyone a
fresh crop of things to do

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:05.453
this weekend,

00:00:05.453 --> 00:00:07.690
and I'll kick it off with
a great app to download.

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:09.220
It's called Storyteller.

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:12.050
If you wake up with 100
social media notifications,

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:15.410
but would rather start your
day with one positive thought,

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:18.330
provoking a daily
affirmation, get this app.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.870
It's curated by the
amazing poet and artist,

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:22.210
Morgan Harper Nichols,

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:24.750
and she shares encouraging
words every morning,

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.240
and beautiful artwork like this one.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.960
No matter what, you will grow,

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:32.240
and it's the perfect addition
to your morning coffee.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:35.950
Okay. Next, I've got
something to listen to.

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.880
It's a podcast called Sleep with Me.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.680
It sounds racy, but it's
literally the opposite.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.240
The whole point of this
very boring podcast,

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:46.410
is to put you to sleep.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:48.480
It's narrated by Drew Scooter Ackerman,

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.140
who bores you to bed with a
short form story or a TV recap,

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:53.720
and each episode lasts an hour,

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:56.110
but you'll only need about 20-
(snoring)

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:57.420
Oh, hi.
(audience laughing)

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:58.970
It's good. It works.

00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:00.520
And to watch,

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:03.660
we have to go with "America's
Funniest Home Videos",

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:05.770
because it's an American classic.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:09.800
And guess who is on the show?

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:13.620
I am so excited because today
we have a very special guest.

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:16.190
He made us laugh for decades,
from "Silver Spoons",

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:17.330
to "The Fresh Prince",

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:20.510
and now he's been hosting
"America's Funniest Home Videos"

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:21.760
for six years.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.308
It's someone I've actually
known since I was a kid.

00:01:25.308 --> 00:01:30.308
Alfonso Ribeiro!
(audience cheering)

00:01:30.844 --> 00:01:32.927
- Hey, how are you, Drew?

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:39.560
- Okay. It must have been
somewhere around like '83,

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:43.600
'84 when we met?

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:48.315
- Yes. "Night of 100 Stars
II", was when we first met,

00:01:48.315 --> 00:01:52.665
back when you were doing,
obviously, "E.T.", and yeah.

00:01:52.665 --> 00:01:55.800
Like I've watched you
grow through the years.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:56.700
You're doing awesome.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:59.574
Congratulations on your
show, it's beautiful.

00:01:59.574 --> 00:02:00.534
- Thank you.
(audience applauding)

00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:01.830
I mean, Alfonso,

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:05.430
I remember going to the
set of "Silver Spoons".

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:07.150
- Right, yep. You would come.

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:10.603
- Yeah, absolutely, and with The Ricker.

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:13.503
Thank you.
(Alfonso laughing)

00:02:13.503 --> 00:02:16.350
- Yes, The Ricker. I haven't
heard that in a long time.

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:18.830
It's been awhile since I've
heard someone refer to him,

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:19.663
as The Ricker.

00:02:19.663 --> 00:02:21.090
- I know, I know.
(audience laughing)

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:24.450
'Cause I met him doing a
cover of People Magazine,

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:26.100
and it was like, you know,

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.280
the fresh crop, or you know,

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:31.610
who's gonna make it out
alive in this photograph,

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:32.650
kind of a thing.
(audience laughing)

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:35.500
And then I knew you in and around,

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:39.980
and then we were both like
in the Corey Feldman circle.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:42.480
- That's, wow. You do remember it all.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:43.313
Yes.

00:02:43.313 --> 00:02:45.320
I wasn't gonna bring up
the Corey Feldman circle,

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:49.060
but yes, we were part of the
Corey Feldman, circle of crazy.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:49.893
- Oh yeah.
(audience laughing)

00:02:49.893 --> 00:02:52.990
No, I remember hanging out
with you in like his kitchen,

00:02:52.990 --> 00:02:55.650
and just getting to be around you,

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.410
and I always liked you so much,

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:59.840
and you were always so like, cool.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:02.390
- Well, you were a sweet little girl,

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:06.100
who has now turned into an
amazing young woman, still.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:08.880
And we had fun. We had
fun back in the day.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:12.150
We were kids in a business that, you know,

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:14.730
wasn't always very kind to us all,

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:17.920
and you know, to be able
to make it out of that,

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:19.580
and remain level-headed,

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:22.710
and be able to continue
doing what we love to do.

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:25.640
Like how many people get to say, you know,

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:30.262
I had my 40th anniversary
in the business last year,

00:03:30.262 --> 00:03:31.760
and that's insane to me,
(audience applauding)

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:35.530
like 40 years being able
to do what we love to do,

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:37.742
and just be in this
business, is very special.

00:03:37.742 --> 00:03:40.740
- And I mean, "America's
Funniest Home Videos"

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:43.473
is such an institution.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:47.219
- Yes, we're on our 31st season,

00:03:47.219 --> 00:03:50.450
my sixth season as host.
(audience applauding)

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:55.450
I get to follow legends like
Tom Bergeron and Bob Saget.

00:03:56.320 --> 00:04:00.040
You know, listen, I feel like
every day it's such an honor

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:03.960
that I get to actually host
that show, especially right now.

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:05.660
Like we all need to laugh,

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:07.780
and "America's Funniest Home Videos"

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:12.510
continues to bring silly
laughter into people's homes,

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:14.680
week in and week out, and you know,

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:16.710
no matter how many times you see someone

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:19.336
get hit in the crotch, it's still funny.

00:04:19.336 --> 00:04:20.730
It's still funny.
(audience laughing)

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:24.210
- It's true. When things go awry, I laugh.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:26.740
I know it's wrong, but I do it.

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:29.250
- Well, see, we make sure, you know,

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:30.620
I always tell people,

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:32.700
you got like a split second to make sure,

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:34.420
when someone falls down
and hurts themselves,

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:37.080
you're like, okay, did they
really hurt themselves?

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:39.256
No. (laughs)
(audience laughing)

00:04:39.256 --> 00:04:42.800
Then full rights to go
ahead and laugh at them,

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:43.780
but they just got to make sure

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:45.467
that they didn't like
break a bone or something,

00:04:45.467 --> 00:04:46.980
before you laugh.

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:50.200
- It's the one second rule.
- Split second.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:51.667
- Yes. Right. The one second.

00:04:51.667 --> 00:04:54.770
One second, they okay? They're
all right. You can laugh.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:55.610
You're good.
(audience laughing)

00:04:55.610 --> 00:05:00.280
- Alfonso, just the best
thing in the world to see you,

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:01.113
really.

00:05:01.113 --> 00:05:02.800
- You too. You too.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:03.633
So happy.

00:05:03.633 --> 00:05:05.420
Thanks for having me on and
being able to chat with you,

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:08.410
and catch up, and we'll do a bunch more.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:10.155
- Yay!
(audience cheering)

00:05:10.155 --> 00:05:11.050
Oh, yay.

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:11.910
And before we go,

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:14.310
I have quick pick from
The Little Yellow Book.

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:15.143
That's right,
(audience applauding)

00:05:15.143 --> 00:05:18.030
it's my weekly list of stuff
that I have to share with you.

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:20.920
This week, this is Blueland,

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:24.030
a company I have been obsessed
with since it came out,

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:27.670
and this, you get a
starter kit for $20 bucks.

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:30.770
You get the powder, you
mix it with the water.

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:33.600
There's this really
feel-good, silicone bottle.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:34.900
And there you go.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:37.150
You are eco-friendly, kissing the earth,

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:39.260
and cleaning your hands and dishes.

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:40.710
They have got everything.

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:41.730
Check them out at,

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:42.640
blueland.com

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:44.507
but all of that will be on our website,

00:05:44.507 --> 00:05:46.270
thedrewbarrymoreshow.com

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:49.334
And that, is your Weekender.
(audience applauding)

00:05:49.334 --> 00:05:52.001
(upbeat music)

